  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Recipes.json|HydeCoBeaversTrimTail": "Trim Beaver Tail",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers": "HydeCo. Beavers!",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers_BeaverCattails": "Cattails on the water",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers_BeaverCattails_tooltip": "Cattails grow on the shallows round every lodge. Cut a clump for cattails: peel the shoots to eat, pull the fluff for tinder and pillow stuffing. A cut clump grows back in a few weeks. Beavers graze them. Off, none grow.",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers_Beavers": "Beavers",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers_BeaversDefendLodge": "Beavers defend themselves",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers_BeaversDefendLodge_tooltip": "Hit a beaver and it turns on you for a while. Take wood from a lodge or chop at it and its beavers come out after you. They bite at your feet and shins; boots and trousers can stop a bite, and a bite never infects. Off, a hit beaver runs for the water and a lodge lets you take its wood.",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers_BeaversNearPlayer": "Most beavers out at once",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers_BeaversNearPlayer_tooltip": "How many beavers can be out around each player at the same time (6 by default); a bigger lodge lets out more. Lower it to see fewer, raise it for more. 0 stops new beavers coming out.",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers_Beavers_tooltip": "Beavers build lodges on wild creeks, rivers, lakes and ponds across the county, never in town. A lodge starts small with two beavers and grows to medium and large with the wood that comes in, some floated down the water and some its beavers gnaw down and carry home, and the bigger it is the more beavers it has room for and lets out. Kits are born in spring into any room left. A lodge with a full store is content: its beavers rest, let you come closer and have bigger litters. A large lodge full of beavers sends a young pair off each spring to start a new lodge on other water. Beavers come out from dusk to dawn, fewer in winter, one at a time by day. A beaver that sees you swims off and dives. Beavers come back from the water with seaweed, stones, waterlogged wood or whatever the river carried down, anything from rope to someone's wallet, and the river snags things in a lodge's sticks that come out with its wood. Take the wood a lodge does not need from it, or break it up with an axe and its beavers flee and never come back. Pull at a lodge and its beavers come out and bite. A dead beaver gives meat, bones and a pelt.",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers_PrepareToRemove": "Prepare to Remove Mod",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers_PrepareToRemove_tooltip": "Removing this mod from a game where a beaver was out at the last save loses the other animals saved around it, your own included. In single player, save once with this version (sleep, or quit) and it should be safe to remove. On a server, turn this on first: no beavers or zombie beavers come out and any that are out go home; let the server save, then remove the mod.",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers_ZombieBeavers": "Zombie beavers",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers_ZombieBeavers_tooltip": "Off by default. On, about one lodge in six is rotten: nothing living comes out of it, a few zombie beavers climb out onto its bank at night and bite anyone who comes close, a dead beaver left lying can get back up as one, and pulling at a rotten lodge or chopping at it brings the whole nest out after you. By day they go back in.",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers_ZombieBiteInfects": "Zombie beaver bites can infect",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoBeavers_ZombieBiteInfects_tooltip": "Off by default: a zombie beaver's bite hurts and never carries the Knox infection. On, a scratch or laceration from one can infect you at the game's own odds.",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Tooltip.json|Tooltip_HydeCoBeavers_BeaverSkull": "The front teeth are orange: iron in the enamel.",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Tooltip.json|Tooltip_HydeCoBeavers_BreakLodgeNeedsAxe": "Needs an axe.",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Tooltip.json|Tooltip_HydeCoBeavers_Cattail": "Peel the shoot to eat it, or pull the fluff from the head for tinder and stuffing.",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Tooltip.json|Tooltip_HydeCoBeavers_CattailFluff": "Catches a spark. Stuffs a pillow.",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoBeavers/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Tooltip.json|Tooltip_HydeCoBeavers_TakeWoodNone": "The beavers need all of its wood, and nothing is caught in it."
}
